From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:53:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(energy): every calorie surface reads the day model
 (hooks marked victor:energy)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- WhoopRepository.resolvedSeries("active_kcal"/"energy_kcal") returns the model's active energy when
  installed: Today's Calories tile and sparkline, Health's Energía activa, Compare, the Workouts heat map.
- TodayScreen and HealthScreen stop preferring the phone's AppleDaily.activeKcal over the series.
- AppViewModel.loadWorkouts and AiCoach.recentWorkoutsBlock publish rows priced by the model
  (EnergyHooks.priced): the Workouts list, its detail, "Total calorías", Today's latest workouts and the
  coach's workouts block all show the model's gross figure.
- AiCoach.buildContext takes the model's active energy per day for its 30-day "active energy" (the
  strap's figure was resting + active); chat, chatStream, the weekly review and "Sugiéreme" pass it.
- CoupledScreen's "Calories" is the model's burn so far for the day shown.
- WorkoutsScreen's detail sheet follows the list, so "Re-estimate" refreshes it while open.
- ProfileStore.isWeightSet / isHeightSet / isBirthSet; NoopApplication installs the model.
- VictorWiringAuditTest: no surface reads activeKcalEst or the phone's activeKcal on its own, every
  calorie surface goes through the model, the old resolver is gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
